    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_17_camera_coherence_design_coherence_rule",
      "label": "Camera coherence rule: preserve the user's view",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-17-camera-coherence-design.md",
      "source_location": "Summary",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": "Tobias Ens (with Claude)",
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "One rule consolidates four separate complaints: the user's view is preserved on every game lifecycle event (start, round advance, end); the reveal animation is the sole place the camera intentionally moves on its own."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_17_camera_coherence_design_initialcameraview_removal",
      "label": "Remove vestigial initialCameraView mode property",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-17-camera-coherence-design.md",
      "source_location": "Item 1",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": "Tobias Ens (with Claude)",
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Per the project memory 'Remove obsolete code and tests', deleting code with no reader is the rule. Both modes effectively become 'preserve', so a field kept only to satisfy an old type contract is dead weight. Commit ordering matters: the reader must be deleted before the property or the typecheck breaks."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_17_camera_coherence_design_line_gradient_reveal",
      "label": "line-gradient reveal animation with easeTo camera",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-17-camera-coherence-design.md",
      "source_location": "Item 3",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": "Tobias Ens (with Claude)",
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Per-frame setData triggers a source/tile rebuild 60x; jumpTo teleports with no interpolation so the hand-computed cubic ease only chose an arc index. Setting the line gradient is a paint update (no re-tiling) and easeTo lets MapLibre interpolate the camera, decoupling smoothness from JS frame jitter. Requires lineMetrics:true for ['line-progress']."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_05_17_camera_coherence_design_reveal_artifact_cleanup",
      "label": "Clear reveal artifacts on round transition",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-17-camera-coherence-design.md",
      "source_location": "Item 4",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": "Tobias Ens (with Claude)",
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Cleanup must mirror setup: whatever the round-ended effect drew, it tears down when status leaves round-ended. clearRevealSources runs unconditionally (mode-neutral) because both country wrong-guesses and city reveals draw the marker+arc; the idle-clear effect stays as a defense-in-depth net."
    }
  ],
